WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.560
Galaktoboureko and baklava are traditional
Greek desserts.

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:14.390
Although several European and Middle Eastern
countries have versions of baklava, most

00:00:14.390 --> 00:00:18.650
consist of phyllo pastry filled with nuts
drenched in honey or syrup.

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:23.750
Galaktoboureko is phyllo filled with custard
and coated with sweet syrup.

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:31.600
This variety of baklava called Berma is made
not with phyllo dough like classic baklava,

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.510
but with kataifi shredded wheat dough.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:41.260
Berma like classic phyllo baklava contains
whole pistachios, never pistachio powder.

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:45.940
This Berma chef pours granulated sugar over
the pistachio kernels.

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:48.550
Next, he sprinkles rosewater.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:51.130
Although this ingredient is optional.

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:57.490
Then syrup made with sugar, water, cinnamon
and nutmeg as well as lemon to prevent the

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.320
sugar from later crystallizing.

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.740
He mixes by hand to thoroughly coat the
kernels.

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:09.460
The kataifi is made of all purpose flour,
milk and water.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:17.860
The chef lays out a section of dough, then
takes a handful of pistachio filling and

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:23.200
places it on the dough, forming a line
running down the middle for a Burma loaf this

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.760
size. The filling is about an inch wide and
high.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:34.610
He folds the end closed and rolls the dough
at an angle down the length of the Burma,

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:37.470
tightly encasing the filling as he goes.

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:42.510
At the end, he folds the opposite end
closed.

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:46.230
It takes a Burma chef months to perfect this
technique.

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:53.920
He places it on a tray to air dry for 24
hours to ensure the dough maintains its

00:01:53.960 --> 00:02:01.220
rolled shape. Unlike classic baklava, which
is baked, Burma is fried, and the risk of

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:06.140
burning the pistachios makes this the most
technically challenging type of baklava to

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:12.980
make. The chef fries the loaves for three
minutes in oil heated to around 350°F,

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:14.870
turning them once per minute.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:18.230
He lets the oil drain off for half an hour.

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:25.430
Then he pours warm, caramelized sugar over
the loaves and lets them soak for 20 minutes.

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:31.370
The sugar to water ratio and the boiling
time of the caramelized sugar have to be just

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:36.650
right. Otherwise it will become either too
hard or too gooey when it cools.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:43.170
After letting the excess drain off the
loaves rest for about three hours.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:51.480
Then the chef rolls the loaf to flatten out
the bumps and slices it into equal pieces.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:00.330
But if there's a protracted battle waging
between your sweet tooth and your willpower.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:06.660
You've got plenty of time to work your way
through a box of Burma because it stays fresh

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:07.860
for two weeks.

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:14.150
To make galaktoboureko.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:18.770
The chef begins with two ingredients milk
and semolina.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:25.430
After bringing the milk to a boil, he
gradually adds the semolina while whisking

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:26.990
and lowering the temperature.

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:30.170
Once the mix thickens, he sets it aside to
cool.

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:39.530
In a separate bowl, the chef whisks eggs,
adds vanilla, then lemon or orange rind.

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:43.640
Other options are orange blossom or
rosewater extract.

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:49.220
He transfers the ingredients to an electric
mixer, adds butter and sugar.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:51.980
Then he adds the semolina and milk mixture.

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:56.680
This mixture must be cool so that the eggs
don't cook.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:03.410
Once everything is thoroughly blended, the
Galaktoboureko custard is ready.

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:09.660
The chef now turns his attention to the
phyllo dough.

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:15.330
He stacks 24 parchment, thin sheets of
phyllo and slices them into squares.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:19.650
He places one scoop full of custard in the
center of each square.

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:25.740
The traditional Greek way is to roll the
squares or bake a large galaktoboureko in a

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:28.310
pan and then cut it into squares.

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:33.300
However, this chef folds over each square to
make Lebanese style triangles.

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:39.750
He douses the top with clarified butter
butter that's been boiled to separate out the

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:42.030
solids and leave just the oil.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:45.300
Then he bakes the pastries for 45 minutes at
325°F.

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:52.200
The golden baked top shines thanks to the
clarified butter.

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:55.980
The chef cooks the same syrup he made for
the baklava.

00:04:56.070 --> 00:05:02.340
Sugar water, cinnamon, nutmeg and lemon and
generously drizzles the mixture all over the

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:07.890
galaktoboureko as he sprinkles on cinnamon
for traditional flavor and some crushed

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:09.900
pistachios for decoration.

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:13.740
Kimchi is Korean comfort food.

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:18.270
The zesty blend of fermented vegetables has
been part of the Korean diet for at least

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:19.570
2000 years.

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:24.600
It's so valued by Koreans that some even
have special refrigerators for it in their

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:30.360
homes. Like fine wine, kimchi must be kept
at a specific temperature to be at its best.

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:36.510
The kitchen staff carves the cabbage into
fairly large strips because cabbage is thin.

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:42.030
Bigger strips will ferment at the same pace
as the shredded carrots and diced scallions.

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:47.940
The next ingredient is ginger, a spice that
will add flavor and soothe the digestive

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:54.530
system. Another worker transfers the
shredded ginger to a porous cotton bag.

00:05:56.630 --> 00:06:02.690
She folds the bag a few times to create a
packet and then places the packet under a

00:06:02.690 --> 00:06:11.900
press. The press squeezes juice from the
ginger and extracts the ginger essence while

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:13.970
leaving the stringy pulp behind.

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:21.110
The worker weighs the ingredients, beginning
with the shredded carrot.

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:23.930
This is the largest ingredient after Napa
cabbage.

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:30.980
She then measures the portion of scallions
that the recipe calls for.

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:35.740
She adds a scoop of Celtic sea salt and
checks the scale.

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:42.090
Other ingredients include crushed garlic.

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:49.190
Chili flakes and the ginger juice.

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:57.170
She stirs the seasonings into the vegetables
and the ginger juice begins to saturate the

00:06:57.170 --> 00:06:58.910
scallion and carrot pieces.

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:05.770
All the ingredients now come together in
this mixer with a big dough hook.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:11.080
The worker adds The carrot and scallion
blend to the Napa cabbage in the base of the

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:18.090
mixing bowl. She activates the mixer and the
dough hook folds all the elements together.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:23.010
Fermentation begins, triggered by the evenly
distributed salt.

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:29.220
Workers, then transfer the mixture to
special fermentation crocks and pack it down.

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:35.260
Two half circle ceramic weights add pressure
to the salted ingredients.

00:07:35.710 --> 00:07:40.870
Juices flow and immerse the kimchi
vegetables, creating an oxygen free

00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:47.380
environment. The salt suppresses the growth
of bad bacteria, allowing the good bacteria

00:07:47.380 --> 00:07:54.190
to flourish. Another worker pours water into
a moat around the lid, creating a ring of

00:07:54.190 --> 00:07:59.440
water that acts as a kind of seal, one that
will keep air out of the crock, but will

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:02.020
allow fermentation gases to escape.

00:08:03.490 --> 00:08:06.400
One week later, the kimchi is sufficiently
fermented.

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:09.940
It is now a living food full of good
bacteria.

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:16.480
A worker packs the kimchi into jars and
weighs each container to confirm that the

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:17.770
amount is correct.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:23.680
The jars must be completely full with no air
space between the kimchi and the lids that

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:25.540
could compromise its shelf life.

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:30.890
She labels the jars and shrink, wraps a
plastic collar around the lids.

00:08:32.690 --> 00:08:37.070
Once refrigerated kimchi can last for up to
14 months.

00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:38.720
Well preserved.

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:41.720
It's practically always ready to be served.

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:50.010
Carlsons are a traditional French candy made
of almonds, candied melon and orange peel.

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:54.140
Topped with a thin layer of hard, typically
white icing.

00:08:54.290 --> 00:08:58.880
The first step in the production is to
rehydrate the almonds with steam for about

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:02.060
ten minutes so that they can be worked into
a paste.

00:09:02.150 --> 00:09:07.880
Once the almonds, moisture content is
increased by 2 to 4%, the almonds pass over a

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:12.560
vibrating screen to drain any water
resulting from steam condensation.

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:16.100
Meanwhile, this cauldron heats up liquid
beet sugar.

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:22.210
France is one of the world's largest sugar
beet producers, so high quality beet sugar is

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:23.380
readily available.

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:30.250
Workers transfer the hydrated almonds to a
grinder and add candied fruit.

00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:33.910
95% melon and 5% orange peel.

00:09:34.180 --> 00:09:37.030
This flavor is the 500 year old traditional
recipe.

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:43.440
Workers grind the ingredients for about ten
minutes until everything is thoroughly

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:45.270
blended into a coarse paste.

00:09:46.470 --> 00:09:51.510
The pace drops onto a conveyor belt, which
transfers it to a kneading machine into which

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:56.880
workers add the hot liquid beet sugar and
natural almond oil made from bitter almonds.

00:09:58.180 --> 00:10:02.260
Kneading blends the ingredients and smooths
the texture of the paste.

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:09.770
A worker boxes the Carlson paste and sets it
aside for three days to let the sugar mature

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:11.120
and stabilize.

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:16.640
Carlsons are topped with an ever so thin
layer of royal icing.

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:21.550
Unlike creamy icings, royal icing is as hard
as a rock.

00:10:22.130 --> 00:10:27.770
To make it. A worker combines icing, sugar
and whipped egg whites passed through a

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:34.150
strainer. A mixer beats the ingredients
until the mixture is thick and smooth, which

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:36.100
typically takes about ten minutes.

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:49.490
After three days of rest, the paste is ready
to be worked.

00:10:50.590 --> 00:10:54.280
Shaping and decorating the collections is a
specialized task.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:58.970
Entrust it to these experienced artisans
called Kali Sanders.

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:04.960
First, they place slices of paste in a press
and load a mold underneath.

00:11:06.820 --> 00:11:10.210
They cover the mold with a wafer thin sheet
of unleavened bread.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:17.700
Then the press piston descends, forcing the
paste with the bread layer underneath into

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:26.400
the mold. They skim off the excess paste,
then fold the stencil over the mold and apply

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:27.900
the layer of royal icing.

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:35.330
They lift off the stencil and push the
buttons which activate the mold pistons.

00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:40.670
Each piston pierces the base of a caisson
and lifts it out of the mold.

00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:47.910
Finally, they remove the Callsigns with
combs designed to fit around the Pistons.

00:11:50.590 --> 00:11:55.450
A ten minute trip through a tunnel oven set
at low temperature bakes the royal icing to a

00:11:55.450 --> 00:11:56.980
hard and shiny state.

00:11:57.460 --> 00:12:02.870
By combining protein and vegetable elements
with rice in a bowl, people have a meal.

00:12:02.890 --> 00:12:07.270
It's Asian comfort food and somehow it just
tastes better in a bowl.

00:12:07.270 --> 00:12:12.010
And people around the world are discovering
the appeal of these one bowl meals.

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:15.620
Asian bowl meals.

00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:17.030
Start with the rice.

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:19.520
Then people add whatever they want.

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:24.260
At food bars like this, there's any number
of choices.

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:29.660
The bowls can be served up fast and the food
is healthy because there are many possible

00:12:29.660 --> 00:12:35.120
combinations. These one bowl meals never get
boring preparation.

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:36.590
Start with the rice.

00:12:36.740 --> 00:12:39.260
This food worker measures enough for 40
portions.

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:45.230
After rinsing the grains repeatedly, he adds
it to a rice cooker.

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:48.770
He then measures the water for cooking.

00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:52.040
He adds it to the cooker.

00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:58.340
It will steam the grains so they cook
uniformly for one hour while the rice is

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:03.500
cooking. The food worker then pours peeled
garlic cloves into a food processor.

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:08.000
He adds A half cup of vegetable oil.

00:13:08.030 --> 00:13:11.780
The garlic will flavor several dishes in the
Asian food bar.

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:18.410
The food processor chops the garlic to a
fine consistency.

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:21.760
Using a mandolin vegetable slicer.

00:13:21.770 --> 00:13:27.030
He slices slivers of carrots along with
chopped onions.

00:13:27.050 --> 00:13:29.420
The carrots will enhance the flavor of fried
rice.

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:34.760
He now removes some rice from the cooker in
order to make fried rice.

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:37.760
He separates the grains so they'll fry more
uniformly.

00:13:42.230 --> 00:13:44.640
The food worker is now ready to fry.

00:13:44.660 --> 00:13:47.750
He heats the wok to a very high temperature.

00:13:47.780 --> 00:13:50.750
He adds cooking oil and it starts to sizzle.

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:57.470
He tosses in the carrot slivers, chopped
onion, garlic and frozen peas.

00:13:57.890 --> 00:14:02.870
He constantly stirs the ingredients and the
flavors sweeten and deepen.

00:14:04.430 --> 00:14:06.800
He turns down the heat a bit and adds the
rice.

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:13.070
He mixes the rice with the other ingredients
as the cooking continues at a slightly lower

00:14:13.070 --> 00:14:18.800
temperature. He measures the temperature for
food safety reasons.

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:22.370
It needs to be over 143°F.

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:26.150
The food worker pours soy sauce onto the hot
wok.

00:14:26.810 --> 00:14:30.800
It trickles down to permeate the rice,
adding flavor and color.

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:34.610
That completes the fried rice component of
the food bar.

00:14:35.420 --> 00:14:37.760
Next up are the vegetable and protein
choices.

00:14:40.220 --> 00:14:43.100
The food worker cube, sushi grade tuna.

00:14:43.310 --> 00:14:45.830
It will be marinated with a spicy sauce
shortly.

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:49.610
He places the tuna in a food bar container.

00:14:51.480 --> 00:14:54.270
He peels cucumber, and then Julie ends it.

00:14:54.390 --> 00:14:59.580
The cucumber will be a raw food choice that
will offset the strong flavor of the tuna.

00:15:01.770 --> 00:15:04.710
The food worker then prepares the tuna spicy
marinade.

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:10.590
He adds chili sauce and a smaller amount of
chili oil to mayonnaise.

00:15:12.390 --> 00:15:13.950
It's hot stuff.

00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:22.300
A seaweed salad dish is another refreshing
choice that will cool the palate.

00:15:23.260 --> 00:15:29.680
He adds the chili mayonnaise to the tuna,
and he turns up the heat a little more with

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:31.390
some extra chili oil.

00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:39.400
A thorough mixing completely saturates the
raw fish with the spicy sauce.

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:44.890
Next, the food worker prepares a dressing
for a cabbage salad.

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:47.620
He starts with a white miso paste.

00:15:47.650 --> 00:15:50.350
A generous amount of soy sauce follows.

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:54.340
Sushi, vinegar and vegetable oil are the
next ingredients.

00:15:55.150 --> 00:15:59.170
After adding some sesame oil, he blends all
the components.

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:02.500
He coats the shredded cabbage with the miso
dressing.

00:16:03.550 --> 00:16:07.270
He sprinkles black sesame seeds onto the
cabbage salad.

00:16:10.180 --> 00:16:12.610
Teriyaki beef is the next option.

00:16:13.750 --> 00:16:18.980
The main ingredients are shaved fillet
steak, chopped ginger and shredded onion.

00:16:19.400 --> 00:16:23.810
The food worker sortase the onion and ginger
to provide a flavor base.

00:16:25.070 --> 00:16:30.380
He adds the shaved steak, and as it cooks,
it takes up the essence of the onion and

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:39.860
ginger. The soy based teriyaki sauce
provides the final layer of flavor.

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:46.470
With this dish now complete, it's time for
the fun part.

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:50.400
Mixing and matching components for the Asian
food bowl.

